/-!
# Orbit divisors in the concrete Held stabilizer chain

The existing ATLAS Schreier words fix successively vertices 0, 1, and 2.
Their orbit at 2 contains 256 points. At the next level we check a stronger
fact than the earlier lower-bound certificate: all the signed generators
preserve the displayed eighteen-point orbit. Its setwise stabilizer inside
the pointwise three-vertex stabilizer is therefore transitive on eighteen
points. Orbit–stabilizer and Lagrange supply a divisor eighteen.

The words and orbit trees below are retained from
`Automorphisms/Normalizer/LowerBound.lean`, generated from
`Automorphisms/Normalizer/Source/lower_words.json` and the unchanged ATLAS
`HeG1-p2058B0` permutations. Every finite identity is checked in the kernel.
This extends those certificates without modifying their shared owner.
The group-theoretic application is the pair bound needed for GLS3 Table 5.3p.
-/

